The combined manuscript gives two separate deterministic algorithms.
Its faster-time construction continues the attributed partial-matching
and deterministic representation framework. Its low-space construction
uses the representation layout, modular-stream viewpoint, and separator
entropy calculation of OpenAI's September 26, 2026 low-space preprint as
starting points. The manuscript proves the deterministic extraction,
prime families, shared covers, interval processing, and resource bounds
used by the new low-space result. The source preprint itself is randomized.
Greedy multi-prime selection through an implicit counting oracle is
credited to Jin, Park, Saha, and Xu, ICALP 2026. These sources are distinct
from the assistance acknowledgment and do not certify the new theorems.
